If I have it right, a boulder trap has a minimum distance of 2 spaces 
between the trap and the boulder (and a maximum of 8). So you could only 
move a boulder 4 to 16 spaces in a straight line. 

You have of course a chance of taking damage when you trigger the trap 
(unless you can arrange for it to be triggered), and also of taking 
damage when you unset (or set?) it unless you move the boulder out of 
the way first in which case the trap would vapourise if triggered 
accidentally. Also, when unsetting there could be a chance that you 
trigger the trap AND succeed in unsetting. That way you might take 
damage and the boulder would also end up where you didn't want it so 
you'ld have to try all over again.



